WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:13.670
A Frenchman walks into a restaurant in Egypt. He doesn t know what he wants to eat. Can

2
00:00:13.670 --> 00:00:21.630
I see a menu? he asks. The Egyptian waiter says, Yes, menu. But he just stands there.

3
00:00:21.630 --> 00:00:30.390
The Frenchman asks, A menu, please? The waiter says, Yes, yes, we have menu. Finally, the

4
00:00:30.390 --> 00:00:36.230
Frenchman stands up and leaves while the waiter tries to understand what happened. What happened

5
00:00:36.230 --> 00:00:42.750
was a false friend. False friends are words that sound the same but mean different things

6
00:00:42.750 --> 00:00:50.550
in different languages. In this case, in French, a menu is a list of food offered at a restaurant.

7
00:00:50.550 --> 00:00:57.910
In Arabic, menu means food. So the Frenchman wanted a list while the poor waiter just wanted

8
00:00:57.910 --> 00:01:05.870
to make him understand that he was in a restaurant. False friends can be very dangerous for language

9
00:01:05.870 --> 00:01:13.830
students. In Spanish, actual means happening currently, not real as it does in English.

10
00:01:13.830 --> 00:01:19.910
To ask in Spanish if something is actually happening means, is it happening now rather

11
00:01:19.910 --> 00:01:26.150
than is it really happening? That s a big difference, especially if you re talking about

12
00:01:26.150 --> 00:01:34.710
a dangerous event. Bra is a funny one. In English, a bra is a kind of underwear. But

13
00:01:34.710 --> 00:01:41.030
in Swedish, it means a good song. Imagine the looks you d get if you walked into a department

14
00:01:41.030 --> 00:01:49.830
store in Sweden and asked for a bra. Demand is another example. In Italian, demand simply

15
00:01:49.830 --> 00:01:57.550
means request. In English, it is more like a command, much more forceful. Imagine walking

16
00:01:57.550 --> 00:02:03.990
into a cafe in the United States and saying, I demand a cup of coffee. You might get hot

17
00:02:03.990 --> 00:02:11.470
coffee spilled all over your lap. False friends aren t really your friend. Be very careful

18
00:02:11.470 --> 00:02:16.750
of words that sound just like words in your language. They may not mean what you think

19
00:02:16.750 --> 00:02:17.390
they do.
